There are a few common ways, depending on what you want to center.

**Center horizontally and vertically (flexbox)** — usually the simplest:

```css
.parent {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: center; /* horizontal */
  align-items: center;     /* vertical */
  min-height: 100vh;       /* or whatever height the parent should fill */
}
```

**Center horizontally only:**

```css
.child {
  margin-inline: auto;
  width: fit-content; /* or a fixed width; auto margins need a width narrower than the parent */
}
```

**Center with grid:**

```css
.parent {
  display: grid;
  place-items: center;
  min-height: 100vh;
}
```

**Center text inside the div** (not the div itself):

```css
.box {
  text-align: center;
}
```

Flexbox or grid on the parent is the usual choice when you want the div itself in the middle of the page or a container.
